	"display_name": "World ambience",
	"description": "P28 (section 4.3's ambience map, the world's rows): the five regions' beds (stereo Ogg loops, non-positional) and the six place beds (mono: the towns, the camps, the giants' hearth, the troll den, the Titan's Bones, the Moot); the emitter loops (the Wend Falls, Hollowmere's pond, the lake shore, the town wells) and the formations' march loop (stomps in step and a drum; class big, priority 75, at most two); the spots (class spot) with volumes balanced from each spot's measured loudness (P23's rule), and three aliases of existing spots at a lower pitch (a rockfall, an old bone's creak, the sunken bell, a mill wheel's creak). Every cue is an Ogg stream on the Ambience bus.",
